# Packing rules for `npm i github:dglazkov/isocan` — the repo is the package.
#
# This file exists to OVERRIDE .gitignore at pack time. `packages/web/dist` is
# gitignored (it is a build artifact) but must ship: the install-time `prepare`
# script builds it, and without it the daemon would serve an empty page. npm
# consults .gitignore only when there is no .npmignore, so the moment this file
# exists the artifact survives.
node_modules
coverage
*.log
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*

# There used to be a `marketing/` exclusion here, and the decision it deferred
# has now been made rather than deleted. That directory was a static page for
# isocan.io carrying a ~500KB screenshot; it was kept out of the pack because
# nobody running `npx isocan setup` needed it, and the note said that when a
# daemon actually served the logged-out surface (phase 14) shipping it would
# become a decision somebody made on purpose.
#
# The daemon serves it now: it IS the app, at `/`, for a browser that is nobody
# yet. So the page ships inside `packages/web/dist` like every other route, and
# what used to be 484KB of PNG is 49KB of WebP at `packages/web/public/front/`
# — small enough that the exclusion is no longer the interesting question.
# `packages/web/test/shot.test.ts` holds that ceiling.
